{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q27293770","formula":"C₄₁H₄₇Cl₂NO₆","hill":"C41H47Cl2NO6","elements":["H","C","N","O","Cl"],"composition":{"C":41.0,"H":47.0,"N":1.0,"O":6.0,"Cl":2.0},"names":{"en":"Atrimustine"},"descriptions":{"en":"Atrimustine (INNTooltip International Nonproprietary Name) (developmental code name KM-2210; former tentative brand name Kregan), also known as bestrabucil or busramustine, is a cytostatic antineoplastic agent which was under development in Japan by Kureha Chemicals (now Kureha Corporation) for the treatment of breast cancer and non-Hodgkin's lymphoma as well as for the prevention of graft-versus-host disease in bone marrow transplant recipients. It is the benzoate ester of an ester conjugate of estradiol and chlorambucil, which results in targeted/site-directed cytostatic activity toward estrogen receptor–positive tissues such as breast and bone."},"fame":2,"pubchemCid":6917688,"mass":720.7,"charge":0,"smiles":"C[C@]12CC[C@H]3[C@H]([C@@H]1CC[C@@H]2OC(=O)COC(=O)CCCC4=CC=C(C=C4)N(CCCl)CCCl)CCC5=C3C=CC(=C5)OC(=O)C6=CC=CC=C6","inchikey":"IFJUINDAXYAPTO-UUBSBJJBSA-N","iupac":"[(8R,9S,13S,14S,17S)-17-[2-[4-[4-[bis(2-chloroethyl)amino]phenyl]butanoyloxy]acetyl]oxy-13-methyl-6,7,8,9,11,12,14,15,16,17-decahydrocyclopenta[a]phenanthren-3-yl] benzoate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"6917688","atoms":97,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":1.092,"y":-0.486,"z":-1.28,"el":"C"},{"x":1.737,"y":-1.895,"z":-1.292,"el":"C"},{"x":2.05,"y":-2.32,"z":0.149,"el":"C"},{"x":3.197,"y":-1.492,"z":0.758,"el":"C"},{"x":4.473,"y":-1.454,"z":-0.124,"el":"C"},{"x":4.13,"y":-1.059,"z":-1.592,"el":"C"},{"x":3.04,"y":-1.997,"z":-2.112,"el":"C"},{"x":2.565,"y":-1.855,"z":-3.555,"el":"C"},{"x":1.188,"y":-2.542,"z":-3.564,"el":"C"},{"x":0.